#> tool: sedrepl
#> wait: 7 kiwis 18 | 8 lemons 22
#> pause: 40
#> must: 1 apples 12 | 2 bananas 30
#> must: 7 kiwis 18 | 8 lemons 22
#> not: 2 bananas 30 | 3 cherries
#> source: s/\n/ | /
# 2. The input stream column. Sheet: "n" and "N" both read the next line; only N keeps both.
# N appends the next input line to the pattern space with a newline between them,
# so s/\n/ | / can join the pair. n would print the current line first and replace
# it. In the table both have "+" under Input Stream; N also has "+" under Pattern Space.
# Try: change N to n and the s/// finds no newline: every line prints on its own.
N
s/\n/ | /

#DATA
1 apples 12
2 bananas 30
3 cherries 7
4 dates 16
5 figs 25
6 grapes 40
7 kiwis 18
8 lemons 22
